      "content": "FLAMSTEAD             LITTLE WOOD END TL 01 SE 4/37 -                                      Nos, 1, and 2                                        Little Wood End Cottages GV                                     II House, now 2 houses. Early C17 or earlier, extended and divided in C19. Timber frame exposed at rear of No.  1 with red brick infill, red tilehanging at front, red brick ground floor, plum brick casing to N-S range. Steep half-hipped old red tile roofs. A Z-shaped 1 1/2-storeys house sub-divided in the middle of the N-S range, N part No. 1, S part No. 2. Casement windows with cast iron frames. Large C17 chimney stack at junction of W wing to main N-S range with 2 conjoined square shafts in Z-plan and moulded cap. Straight-brace and exposed framing in N wall of this  W  wing.  Clasped-purlin  roof  with  straight  windbraces  and squint-butted Scarf joint in wallplate.  Large 3-centred chamfered arched brick open fireplace on 1st floor of N-S range. Gabled dormers to No. 2 on W and on lower E wing. Listing NGR: TL0575413870"
    }
  ],
